      "extract": "We now turn to a seemingly unrelated field of moduli of quiver representations. A quiver $Q$ is an oriented graph with a finite set of vertices $Q_0$ and finitely many arrows between vertices $\\alpha:i\\rightarrow j$. On ${\\bf Z}Q_0$, we define the Euler form of $Q$ by $\\langle {\\bm d},{\\bm e}\\rangle_Q=\\sum_{i\\in Q_0}d_ie_i-\\sum_{\\alpha:i\\rightarrow j}d_ie_j.$ A quiver representation assigns to each vertex $i\\in Q_0$",
      "extractCut": true
    },
