      ],
      "extract": "We present now our main claim, which is the statement that various types of knot invariants, for a given knot, are encoded in the data of moduli spaces of quiver representations of a certain quiver, assigned to this knot. As explained in the introduction, from physical perspective this is a consequence of the supersymmetric quiver quantum mechanics description of BPS states in brane systems representing knots.",
